        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Steve Sekely, King Baggot, Gail Patrick, Nancy Kelly\n- Films: Women in Bondage, The Gaiety Girl\n- Concepts: alternate names, publicity titles, lost films\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Sekely was born Székely István and was known by several names, including Stefan Szekely, reflecting changes in his professional and immigration status.\n- King Baggot was the first individually publicized leading man in America.\n- King Baggot was referred to as \"King of the Movies,\" \"The Most Photographed Man in the World,\" and \"The Man Whose Face Is As Familiar As The Man In The Moon.\"\n- The Gaiety Girl is a lost 1924 silent romantic film directed by King Baggot.\n- Women in Bondage was directed by Steve Sekely and starred Gail Patrick and Nancy Kelly.",
